<A NAME=S10></A>
<H2>Summary</H2>
<UL>
<LI>vCard (a card per person, <CODE>NAME;PARAMETERS:value</CODE> lines) and CSV (rows of comma-separated
values, with a header row) are how contacts pass between programs.<P>
<LI>RISC OS 3.71 uses Latin-1; other programs use UTF-8. Decode files with <CODE>TextDecoder</CODE>, turning
characters RISC OS can't show into <CODE>?</CODE>; encode exported files as UTF-8.<P>
<LI>Keep file formats in functions of text only, and test them.<P>
<LI><CODE>'dataload'</CODE> brings dropped files; <CODE>'datasave'</CODE> and <CODE>ev.receive()</CODE>
bring data straight from another program.<P>
<LI>Save in your own format; export others with Save boxes of their own; <CODE>dragSave</CODE> lets the user
drag data out of a window.<P>
<LI><CODE>x ??= y</CODE> sets <CODE>x</CODE> only if it has no value; <CODE>const [a, b] = array</CODE>
takes an array apart.<P>
</UL>

